# serializer version: 1
# name: test_assistant_pane_welcome_copy
  '''
  Hi! I'm PostHog, an AI agent. Ask me about your product data, or tell me what to fix and I'll open a pull request in a connected repo.
  • Keep replying here while I'm working and I'll pick up what you say.
  • Want a different model? Say so: `use fable for this one`.
  • Answering from the wrong project? Name the one you want: `give me DAU for Staging please`.
  • Hit the thumbs under my replies when I get something wrong.
  '''
# ---
# name: test_welcome_copy[channel]
  '''
  Hey, I'm PostHog. Tag me with @PostHog to get started.
  
  ---
  
  :wave: Hey, I'm PostHog. Tag me with `@PostHog` and I'll dig into your product data, poke around your codebase, or open a pull request to fix something.
  
  *Try asking me*
  • `@PostHog why did signups drop in the EU last week?`
  • `@PostHog open a PR that adds a unit test for src/utils.py`
  
  *A few things worth knowing*
  • Tag me again in the thread while I'm working and I'll pick up what you say.
  • Want a different model? Say so: `@PostHog use fable for this one`, or `@PostHog run this on opus 5 at high effort`.
  • Answering from the wrong project? Name the one you want: `@PostHog give me DAU for Staging please`. `/posthog project` shows your default.
  • You can DM me instead of tagging me here.
  
  *Tell me when I get it wrong*
  Hit the thumbs under my replies. A thumbs down asks what went wrong, and that goes straight to the team building me. You can also react with :thumbsup: or :thumbsdown:.
  
  I also unfurl PostHog links shared in this channel. `/posthog` lists my commands, and your default model and thread follow-ups live in <slack://app?team=T_WELCOME&id=A_WELCOME&tab=home|my Home tab>.
  
  [Read the docs](https://posthog.com/docs/slack-app)
  '''
# ---
# name: test_welcome_copy[team_join]
  '''
  Hey, welcome! I'm PostHog. Message me to get started.
  
  ---
  
  :wave: Hey, welcome! I'm PostHog, an AI agent your team already uses here. Message me, or tag `@PostHog` in any channel, and I'll dig into your product data or open a pull request in a connected repo.
  
  *Try asking me*
  • `why did signups drop in the EU last week?`
  • `fix the flaky billing CI job`
  
  *A few things worth knowing*
  • Keep replying in the thread while I'm working and I'll pick up what you say. In a channel, tag me in the reply.
  • Want a different model? Say so: `use fable for this one`.
  
  *Tell me when I get it wrong*
  Hit the thumbs under my replies. A thumbs down asks what went wrong, and that goes straight to the team building me. You can also react with :thumbsup: or :thumbsdown:.
  
  In a channel, `/posthog` lists my commands. Your default model, thread follow-ups and linked accounts live in <slack://app?team=T_WELCOME&id=A_WELCOME&tab=home|my Home tab>.
  
  [Read the docs](https://posthog.com/docs/slack-app)
  '''
# ---
# name: TestOnboardingDm.test_onboarding_dm_copy
  '''
  Set up PostHog - self-driving for your product
  
  ---
  
  👋 *Hi, I'm PostHog - self-driving for your product*
  I'm an AI agent on autopilot: I watch your product for problems, investigate them myself, and open pull requests to fix them - so issues get handled before they reach your backlog.
  
  💬 *You can also just talk to me*
  Tag `@PostHog` in any channel, or message me here, to dig into your product data or open a pull request. Name a project to route one question: `@PostHog give me DAU for Staging please`. In a channel, `/posthog` lists my commands.
  
  ---
  
  *1. Connect your codebase* :wrench:
  Connect GitHub so I can fix things, not just flag them - when I spot a problem in your product I'll proactively open a pull request with the fix for you to review.
  
  [Connect GitHub](http://localhost:8010/integrations/connect/github/?project_id=<team_id>&connect_from=slack)
  
  *2. Choose what I watch* :eyes:
  Tick the signals I should monitor and investigate.
  
  [ ] *Error tracking*: new, reopened & spiking issues
  
  *3. Where I report* :inbox_tray:
  Everything I find lands in one shared channel so the team stays in the loop.
  
  [Create #posthog-inbox](slack_inbox_create)
  
  🎉 Once you're set up, I'll start watching your product and send your first report to #posthog-inbox as soon as I spot something.
  
  👍 Hit the thumbs under my replies when I get something wrong. Your default model and linked accounts live in my Home tab.
  '''
# ---
